# 10. SIGNATURE END-TO-END WORKFLOW

Implement this complete workflow.

STEP 1:
An authorized institution user creates an application.

STEP 2:
The user uploads multiple supporting documents.

STEP 3:
The system validates file formats and stores the documents securely.

STEP 4:
The document-processing service extracts text and classifies each document.

STEP 5:
The extraction service stores structured fields and their source-page references.

STEP 6:
The validation engine runs the applicable configured rules.

STEP 7:
The cross-document engine compares relevant extracted fields.

STEP 8:
The evidence graph links findings to source documents and applicable rules.

STEP 9:
The verification adapter attempts supported source verification.

STEP 10:
Unresolved mismatches and uncertain findings enter the appropriate review queue.

STEP 11:
The authorized reviewer examines the evidence and records an action.

STEP 12:
The institution receives a request for additional evidence if required and permitted.

STEP 13:
The institution submits the requested evidence.

STEP 14:
The relevant validation checks run again.

STEP 15:
The system generates an updated report and preserves the history of earlier findings and actions.

STEP 16:
The competent authority retains responsibility for any formal regulatory decision.

Every step must persist its results.

